1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,180
If your knee replacement still hurts

2
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:04,940
and the X-ray keeps coming back fine,

3
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:06,920
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:08,380
I've been driving a tow truck

5
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:09,870
for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:11,210
In and out of the cab,

7
00:00:11,210 --> 00:00:13,210
crouching down to hook up cars,

8
00:00:13,210 --> 00:00:14,410
day and night.

9
00:00:14,410 --> 00:00:15,310
I had my right knee

10
00:00:15,310 --> 00:00:16,930
replaced two years ago.

11
00:00:16,930 --> 00:00:19,180
It has hurt every day since.

12
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:20,380
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:21,400
I know what that felt like,

14
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:22,400
and it went away.

15
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:23,650
This is different.

16
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:24,220
Tight.

17
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:24,980
Full.

18
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:25,890
Like a band around

19
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:27,830
the joint that never loosens.

20
00:00:27,830 --> 00:00:28,750
And for two years I've

21
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:30,170
been told the same thing.

22
00:00:30,170 --> 00:00:31,310
Give it time.

23
00:00:31,310 --> 00:00:32,920
At six weeks it was swelling,

24
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:34,510
and swelling is normal.

25
00:00:34,510 --> 00:00:36,340
At three months, give it six.

26
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:37,510
At six months,

27
00:00:37,510 --> 00:00:39,300
some knees take a full year.

28
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:42,280
At a year, eighteen months isn't unusual.

29
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,530
And I didn't just wait.

30
00:00:43,530 --> 00:00:45,230
We went down the list.

31
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:46,650
More physical therapy.

32
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:49,220
Every session, every exercise at home.

33
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:50,460
I got stronger.

34
00:00:50,460 --> 00:00:52,100
The tightness never moved.

35
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:53,570
The pain pills helped,

36
00:00:53,570 --> 00:00:55,220
and that was the problem.

37
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:57,380
I'm already on enough every morning,

38
00:00:57,380 --> 00:00:58,380
and nobody could tell me

39
00:00:58,380 --> 00:00:59,950
when I'd get to stop.

40
00:00:59,950 --> 00:01:01,220
Then a nerve block.

41
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,170
Then talk of burning the nerve.

42
00:01:03,170 --> 00:01:04,140
And after that,

43
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:05,660
a second operation to go back

44
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:07,180
in and do it over.

45
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:08,400
I said no.

46
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,660
Every morning I climbed up

47
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:10,710
into the cab

48
00:01:10,710 --> 00:01:11,730
and my knee felt like

49
00:01:11,730 --> 00:01:13,530
a band was wrapped around it,

50
00:01:13,530 --> 00:01:15,940
tightening every inch I tried to straighten.

51
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:17,810
Every morning I took something for it

52
00:01:17,810 --> 00:01:19,300
and took the next call.

53
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:20,850
Couldn't do the stairs,

54
00:01:20,850 --> 00:01:22,090
couldn't stand at the counter

55
00:01:22,090 --> 00:01:23,940
long enough to finish dinner,

56
00:01:23,940 --> 00:01:26,050
couldn't sit through my granddaughter's game

57
00:01:26,050 --> 00:01:28,420
without shifting every two minutes.

58
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:29,690
Every time I crouched down

59
00:01:29,690 --> 00:01:30,830
to hook up a car,

60
00:01:30,830 --> 00:01:32,420
I had to grab the bumper

61
00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:33,750
to get back up.

62
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:35,610
The other drivers started taking

63
00:01:35,610 --> 00:01:36,850
my night calls.

64
00:01:36,850 --> 00:01:38,820
Nobody said anything.

65
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:40,400
It woke me at night,

66
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:41,920
and it turned ordinary things,

67
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:43,160
like getting in the truck

68
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:44,750
or up off the couch,

69
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:46,220
into a decision.

70
00:01:46,220 --> 00:01:48,070
After a long and serious talk

71
00:01:48,070 --> 00:01:49,790
with my wife, I went back

72
00:01:49,790 --> 00:01:51,370
in one more time.

73
00:01:51,370 --> 00:01:52,500
That was the fourth set

74
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:54,290
of X-rays on this knee.

75
00:01:54,290 --> 00:01:56,170
And like the three before it,

76
00:01:56,170 --> 00:01:58,930
the answer was everything looks great.

77
00:01:58,930 --> 00:02:02,020
No loosening, no infection, nothing wrong.

78
00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:03,180
Only this time there

79
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:04,680
was no new number.

80
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,860
Nobody said give it another six months.

81
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:08,530
There was nothing left to give it.

82
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:09,530
I sat in the parking lot

83
00:02:09,530 --> 00:02:10,800
for a while.

84
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:11,920
Okay, I thought.

85
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:13,460
Then explain this.

86
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:15,580
Anyway, a couple of months back,

87
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:17,380
I hit my breaking point.

88
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:19,640
It was around 2:30 in the morning.

89
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:21,650
Everyone in the house was asleep

90
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:23,380
and I was downstairs in the recliner

91
00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:24,500
with my leg up,

92
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:25,980
trying to find any angle

93
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:26,750
where it didn't feel

94
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:28,070
like something was wrapped around

95
00:02:28,070 --> 00:02:30,170
my knee and tightening.

96
00:02:30,170 --> 00:02:32,680
My wife didn't know I'd come downstairs.

97
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:34,490
By then I'd stopped telling her.

98
00:02:34,490 --> 00:02:35,500
And I just thought,

99
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:37,030
is this really my life now?

100
00:02:37,030 --> 00:02:38,510
I can't live like this.

101
00:02:38,510 --> 00:02:40,150
So I made myself a promise.

102
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:40,830
I wouldn't go a day

103
00:02:40,830 --> 00:02:42,560
without looking for an answer.

104
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:44,030
And when I found one,

105
00:02:44,030 --> 00:02:45,060
I'd share it with everyone

106
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:46,350
going through the same thing.

107
00:02:46,350 --> 00:02:47,560
So I got my laptop out

108
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:48,360
and went looking.

109
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,720
Not for a product.

110
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:51,350
For an explanation.

111
00:02:51,350 --> 00:02:52,840
Mayo Clinic forums,

112
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:55,170
the knee replacement group on Facebook,

113
00:02:55,170 --> 00:02:57,930
doctor videos, medical animations.

114
00:02:57,930 --> 00:02:58,720
And that's when I found

115
00:02:58,720 --> 00:02:59,320
a video from

116
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,780
a physical therapist named Dr.

117
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:02,880
Steven Salinger, whose own wife

118
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:04,790
had been through exactly this.

119
00:03:04,790 --> 00:03:06,520
But before I say anything else,

120
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:08,470
I want to be straight with you.

121
00:03:08,470 --> 00:03:11,000
You've already had something work fast.

122
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:11,590
The ice.

123
00:03:11,590 --> 00:03:13,480
The first week of a new pill.

124
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:15,350
The good day after a session.

125
00:03:15,350 --> 00:03:16,680
Then it wore off.

126
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:19,020
That's the part nobody warns you about.

127
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:21,020
Fast relief isn't relief.

128
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:22,470
It's a preview.

129
00:03:22,470 --> 00:03:23,040
So I'm not going

130
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,600
to tell you this works fast.

131
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:25,600
It doesn't.

132
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,070
But if you're willing to be patient,

133
00:03:27,070 --> 00:03:28,050
and to look at what's going

134
00:03:28,050 --> 00:03:29,130
on around your new knee

135
00:03:29,130 --> 00:03:30,780
instead of inside it, there is

136
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:33,370
a real reason it still hurts.

137
00:03:33,370 --> 00:03:35,230
And something you can do about it.

138
00:03:35,230 --> 00:03:36,500
Let me explain what he said,

139
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:37,340
because this is what

140
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:38,940
changed everything for me.

141
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:40,670
He started with the basics.

142
00:03:40,670 --> 00:03:42,060
A knee replacement takes out

143
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:43,580
the worn joint surfaces

144
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:45,420
and puts in metal and plastic.

145
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:47,210
That's what stops the arthritis pain

146
00:03:47,210 --> 00:03:49,020
you had before the operation.

147
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:50,590
That part I already knew.

148
00:03:50,590 --> 00:03:51,880
But then he explained something

149
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:53,590
nobody had ever told me.

150
00:03:53,590 --> 00:03:54,760
He said, think about

151
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:56,660
a swollen foot inside a shoe.

152
00:03:56,660 --> 00:03:58,240
The shoe didn't shrink.

153
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:00,460
Your foot is taking up more room,

154
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:02,240
so everything feels cramped

155
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:04,200
and tight and squeezed.

156
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,370
Your new knee sits

157
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:06,480
in a limited space

158
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:09,300
with living tissue packed all around it.

159
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,170
To put that knee

160
00:04:10,170 --> 00:04:11,560
in, the surgeon had

161
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:13,400
to work through that tissue.

162
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:16,150
Afterwards it gets inflamed and swollen.

163
00:04:16,150 --> 00:04:17,860
At first that's normal.

164
00:04:17,860 --> 00:04:19,000
But in some people

165
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,860
that swelling can stay switched

166
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:23,810
on far longer than expected.

167
00:04:23,810 --> 00:04:26,160
And swollen tissue takes up more room

168
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:27,940
than calm tissue does.

169
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:29,160
So when you bend,

170
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:31,360
that tissue gets compressed.

171
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:33,810
When you straighten, it gets pulled tight.

172
00:04:33,810 --> 00:04:34,910
That's the band.

173
00:04:34,910 --> 00:04:37,380
That's the ache that never quite leaves.

174
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:38,360
And you start being

175
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,560
the one who says,

176
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:40,630
you go ahead.

177
00:04:40,630 --> 00:04:41,820
I'll stay here.

178
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:43,110
And that's exactly why

179
00:04:43,110 --> 00:04:43,890
so much of what

180
00:04:43,890 --> 00:04:45,920
I'd tried hadn't worked.

181
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,570
Physical therapy strengthens

182
00:04:47,570 --> 00:04:49,200
the muscles around the knee.

183
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:51,380
Worth doing, and I'd done it.

184
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:52,470
It does nothing about

185
00:04:52,470 --> 00:04:54,070
tissue taking up room.

186
00:04:54,070 --> 00:04:55,240
A nerve block quiets

187
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:57,070
the nerve carrying the signal.

188
00:04:57,070 --> 00:04:59,430
It doesn't touch what's generating it.

189
00:04:59,430 --> 00:05:00,660
But when that irritated

190
00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:02,460
tissue finally calms down,

191
00:05:02,460 --> 00:05:04,060
it holds less fluid,

192
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:06,010
and it takes up less room.

193
00:05:06,010 --> 00:05:07,970
Less room taken up means

194
00:05:07,970 --> 00:05:10,300
less pressure squeezing the joint.

195
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:12,550
That's what takes the pressure off.

196
00:05:12,550 --> 00:05:14,050
After two years of this,

197
00:05:14,050 --> 00:05:16,030
it finally made sense.

198
00:05:16,030 --> 00:05:18,070
The problem was never the new knee.

199
00:05:18,070 --> 00:05:20,350
It was the tissue crowded around it.

200
00:05:20,350 --> 00:05:21,970
He calls it the squeeze.

201
00:05:21,970 --> 00:05:24,710
Once you've felt it, that's the word.

202
00:05:24,710 --> 00:05:26,200
I'd bought knee sleeves,

203
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:28,500
compression braces, creams,

204
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,350
half of Amazon really,

205
00:05:30,350 --> 00:05:31,360
and all any of it

206
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,990
gave me was an hour.

207
00:05:32,990 --> 00:05:34,080
I even looked at going

208
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:36,070
to a clinic for the light therapy.

209
00:05:36,070 --> 00:05:38,140
But at $200 a session

210
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:39,950
with nothing covered by insurance,

211
00:05:39,950 --> 00:05:41,330
that was a quick no.

212
00:05:41,330 --> 00:05:42,650
Then one night I went back

213
00:05:42,650 --> 00:05:43,990
to that knee replacement group

214
00:05:43,990 --> 00:05:45,460
and actually read it.

215
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:46,780
Thousands of people,

216
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:48,440
years out from surgery,

217
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:49,850
comparing notes on stiffness

218
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:52,570
and tightness nobody could explain.

219
00:05:52,570 --> 00:05:54,230
And no matter how far I scrolled,

220
00:05:54,230 --> 00:05:56,070
the same thing kept coming up.

221
00:05:56,070 --> 00:05:58,090
This one device,

222
00:05:58,090 --> 00:05:59,120
and people saying it was

223
00:05:59,120 --> 00:05:59,800
the first thing

224
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:01,310
that made a difference.

225
00:06:01,310 --> 00:06:03,560
And before anyone jumps in thinking,

226
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,830
alright, here it comes,

227
00:06:04,830 --> 00:06:06,190
he's selling me something,

228
00:06:06,190 --> 00:06:06,700
let me shut

229
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,030
that down right now.

230
00:06:08,030 --> 00:06:08,530
I'm only here

231
00:06:08,530 --> 00:06:10,050
because I made myself a promise

232
00:06:10,050 --> 00:06:11,710
at 2:30 in the morning that

233
00:06:11,710 --> 00:06:12,870
if I ever found something

234
00:06:12,870 --> 00:06:15,270
that helped, I'd say so.

235
00:06:15,270 --> 00:06:16,800
It's called the KenRelief

236
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:18,690
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

237
00:06:18,690 --> 00:06:20,800
At first glance I didn't buy it.

238
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:21,470
It looked like

239
00:06:21,470 --> 00:06:23,710
the cheap knee sleeves off Amazon

240
00:06:23,710 --> 00:06:25,480
that did nothing for me.

241
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:27,460
But I went to their website anyway,

242
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:28,380
just to see what all

243
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:29,780
the fuss was about.

244
00:06:29,780 --> 00:06:31,080
It's the same red light

245
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:33,130
therapy clinics charge $200

246
00:06:33,130 --> 00:06:35,300
a session for, off machines

247
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:37,340
that cost fifty thousand dollars,

248
00:06:37,340 --> 00:06:38,420
in a wrap you plug

249
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:39,910
into the wall at home.

250
00:06:39,910 --> 00:06:41,750
Two hundred and forty lights.

251
00:06:41,750 --> 00:06:44,290
Red at 660 nanometers

252
00:06:44,290 --> 00:06:46,950
and near-infrared at 850,

253
00:06:46,950 --> 00:06:49,460
run together for the strongest effect.

254
00:06:49,460 --> 00:06:51,080
Four strength levels.

255
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:53,030
A five to thirty minute timer.

256
00:06:53,030 --> 00:06:54,620
Then I saw the guarantee.

257
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:55,870
Ninety days.

258
00:06:55,870 --> 00:06:57,760
Results or your money back,

259
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:00,360
no questions, no store credit,

260
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:02,330
and you don't even send it back.

261
00:07:02,330 --> 00:07:04,360
No physical therapist ever gave me

262
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:06,500
ninety days to change my mind.

263
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:07,980
There wasn't much to lose,

264
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:09,050
so I ordered it.

265
00:07:09,050 --> 00:07:10,490
Two of them, actually.

266
00:07:10,490 --> 00:07:12,450
Only the right knee was replaced,

267
00:07:12,450 --> 00:07:13,550
but you favor the leg

268
00:07:13,550 --> 00:07:15,060
that hurts, and I'd done it

269
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,130
in and out of that cab

270
00:07:16,130 --> 00:07:17,510
for two years.

271
00:07:17,510 --> 00:07:20,120
The left one was carrying the difference.

272
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,200
When it came,

273
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:23,540
I strapped it on expecting nothing,

274
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:24,730
because I'd been let down

275
00:07:24,730 --> 00:07:27,060
too many times to get excited.

276
00:07:27,060 --> 00:07:28,850
What I felt was warmth.

277
00:07:28,850 --> 00:07:31,000
Not a heating pad kind of hot.

278
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,050
More like it was coming

279
00:07:32,050 --> 00:07:33,380
from inside the knee

280
00:07:33,380 --> 00:07:34,960
and spreading around it.

281
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:36,250
And that was it.

282
00:07:36,250 --> 00:07:38,090
That was the whole experience.

283
00:07:38,090 --> 00:07:39,240
When I took it off,

284
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:39,920
I'll be honest,

285
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:41,800
nothing dramatic had happened.

286
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:43,930
And after what that video said,

287
00:07:43,930 --> 00:07:46,200
that's exactly what I expected.

288
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:47,670
What was different was

289
00:07:47,670 --> 00:07:48,690
that for the first time

290
00:07:48,690 --> 00:07:50,840
in two years I'd done something for

291
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:53,230
my knee instead of to it.

292
00:07:53,230 --> 00:07:55,230
Twenty minutes, in my own chair,

293
00:07:55,230 --> 00:07:56,210
after my shift.

294
00:07:56,210 --> 00:07:57,920
No drive, no copay.

295
00:07:57,920 --> 00:07:59,590
They say twenty minutes.

296
00:07:59,590 --> 00:08:01,770
I did thirty, twice a day,

297
00:08:01,770 --> 00:08:03,780
lowest setting that first week.

298
00:08:03,780 --> 00:08:05,610
I put it on the calendar.

299
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:06,620
The first week,

300
00:08:06,620 --> 00:08:07,630
I couldn't have told you

301
00:08:07,630 --> 00:08:09,080
if anything was happening.

302
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:10,040
I tried not to get

303
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:11,030
my hopes up.

304
00:08:11,030 --> 00:08:12,020
I'd had things help for

305
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:13,460
a week and then stop.

306
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:14,750
But somewhere in the second

307
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:16,210
week I noticed I'd come down

308
00:08:16,210 --> 00:08:18,580
the stairs without holding the rail.

309
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:20,120
I hadn't decided to.

310
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:21,330
I just did it,

311
00:08:21,330 --> 00:08:22,740
then stopped halfway down

312
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:24,340
because I realized.

313
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:25,270
By the end of the fourth

314
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:26,560
week I'd slept through

315
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:28,490
the night four times running.

316
00:08:28,490 --> 00:08:29,490
I stood at the counter

317
00:08:29,490 --> 00:08:30,900
and finished making dinner

318
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:32,780
without looking for the stool.

319
00:08:32,780 --> 00:08:34,450
None of that is dramatic.

320
00:08:34,450 --> 00:08:35,410
All of it was gone

321
00:08:35,410 --> 00:08:36,840
for two years.

322
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:38,510
A few weeks later my wife asked

323
00:08:38,510 --> 00:08:39,390
if I wanted to walk

324
00:08:39,390 --> 00:08:41,510
the long way around the block.

325
00:08:41,510 --> 00:08:42,390
And for the first time

326
00:08:42,390 --> 00:08:44,300
in two years, I said yes.

327
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:46,040
I wanted to understand why,

328
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:48,080
so I read the whole thing.

329
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,740
It comes down to four steps.

330
00:08:49,740 --> 00:08:50,800
One.

331
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:52,040
The tissue around a new

332
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:53,970
knee can stay inflamed long

333
00:08:53,970 --> 00:08:55,670
after surgery is over.

334
00:08:55,670 --> 00:08:56,700
Two.

335
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:59,160
Inflamed tissue holds extra fluid,

336
00:08:59,160 --> 00:09:00,310
so it takes up more room

337
00:09:00,310 --> 00:09:01,440
than it should.

338
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:01,900
Three.

339
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:04,270
There's only so much room in there.

340
00:09:04,270 --> 00:09:05,920
Bending compresses it.

341
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,420
Straightening pulls it tight.

342
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:08,840
That's the squeeze.

343
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:09,730
Four.

344
00:09:09,730 --> 00:09:12,210
Red and near-infrared light have been studied

345
00:09:12,210 --> 00:09:14,080
for calming that inflammation,

346
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:15,460
so the swelling and the pressure

347
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:16,940
can come down with it.

348
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:18,680
In a randomized trial,

349
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:20,530
patients given light therapy after

350
00:09:20,530 --> 00:09:23,130
a knee replacement had less pain,

351
00:09:23,130 --> 00:09:25,540
less swelling and better early movement

352
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:26,860
than those who weren't.

353
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:29,600
A 2025 review said the same,

354
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,230
and was clear

355
00:09:30,230 --> 00:09:32,120
the evidence is still limited.

356
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:33,090
I probably sound like

357
00:09:33,090 --> 00:09:34,690
a broken record to my family

358
00:09:34,690 --> 00:09:36,280
and the other drivers.

359
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:38,150
But after two years of doing

360
00:09:38,150 --> 00:09:39,880
everything I was told

361
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:41,350
and getting nowhere,

362
00:09:41,350 --> 00:09:42,990
you have no idea what it's

363
00:09:42,990 --> 00:09:44,720
like to sleep through the night,

364
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:46,450
say yes to the walk,

365
00:09:46,450 --> 00:09:48,040
and get my life back.

366
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:49,400
So take it from me.

367
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,890
Don't spend another year waiting

368
00:09:50,890 --> 00:09:52,010
for it to settle.

369
00:09:52,010 --> 00:09:54,110
Don't spend two hundred a session.

370
00:09:54,110 --> 00:09:55,330
More than ten thousand people

371
00:09:55,330 --> 00:09:56,470
with pain after a knee

372
00:09:56,470 --> 00:09:58,810
replacement have already tried this.

373
00:09:58,810 --> 00:10:00,750
Some had it worse than I did.

374
00:10:00,750 --> 00:10:02,380
You can get the KenRelief wrap

375
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:03,750
from their website,

376
00:10:03,750 --> 00:10:04,880
with a discount link

377
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:06,640
and ninety days to try it.

378
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:08,770
If it doesn't do anything for you,

379
00:10:08,770 --> 00:10:09,980
you get your money back

380
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:11,310
and you keep the wrap.

381
00:10:11,310 --> 00:10:12,040
They only release

382
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:13,770
so many at that price.

383
00:10:13,770 --> 00:10:15,900
If it's still there, get one,

384
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:17,570
